{{!--
  Course enquiry form, rendered at the foot of every course page.

  All seven pages use the SAME form name, so Netlify registers one form and
  every submission carries a hidden `course` field saying which page it came
  from — one inbox and one notification to configure, not seven. The course
  value is baked in at build time from the model's `crumb`, so no query
  string and no JavaScript is involved.

  The fields are the five Gaynor asked for after reading a test submission —
  name, email, mobile, dog's name, dog's age — plus an optional free-text box.
  All five are required: the mobile number because she adds people to the
  class WhatsApp group, which is why the field says so rather than leaving the
  visitor to wonder. Breed is deliberately absent; she did not ask for it, and
  it is a behavioural consultation's question rather than a course enquiry's.

  The five sit in two <fieldset> blocks — the person, then the dog — because a
  single flat two-column grid put "Mobile number" and "Your dog's name" side by
  side, so the eye had no way to tell which questions were about whom. The
  fieldset/legend pairing is what carries that grouping to a screen reader too,
  which a pair of headings and <div>s would not.

  Inputs keep the site's global :focus-visible ring rather than the
  `focus-visible:outline-none` the older form on /contact/ uses — that
  override drops the two-layer indicator the design system defines, and axe
  does not catch non-text contrast (see CLAUDE.md).

  Labels carry no "*" and no screen-reader-only "required" text: Netlify
  derives each field's display name in the dashboard and the notification
  email from the <label>'s text, so that markup arrived as "Your name
  required". The `required` attribute already conveys the same thing to a
  screen reader, and the two optional fields say so in their own help text.
--}}
<section id="enquire" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 rounded-card border border-sand-200 bg-white p-6 sm:p-8">
  <h2 class="mb-2 font-display text-xl text-ink-900">Ask about {{model.crumb}}</h2>

  <p class="mb-6 text-ink-600">
    {{#if model.enquiryLead}}
      {{model.enquiryLead}}
    {{else}}
      Tell Gaynor a little about your dog and she will come back to you with
      whether this is the right course to start on.
    {{/if}}
  </p>

  <form name="course-enquiry" method="POST" action="{{link "thanks" canonical=true}}" data-netlify="true"
    netlify-honeypot="bot-field" data-enquiry class="grid gap-6">

    {{!-- Netlify pairs a submission to its form by this field. --}}
    <input type="hidden" name="form-name" value="course-enquiry">
    {{!-- Which page the enquiry came from. Baked in at build time. --}}
    <input type="hidden" name="course" value="{{model.crumb}}">
    {{!-- Netlify uses a field literally named `subject` as the notification
          email's subject line. This static value is the no-JavaScript
          fallback; /js/site.js rewrites it on submit to include the sender's
          name, because Gmail threads messages sharing a subject and a
          course-only subject would collapse every enquiry about the same
          course, from different people, into one conversation. The prefix is
          the model's `enquiryKind` where it has one (the consultation pages
          render this same form), so one inbox still sorts at a glance — and
          site.js re-derives that prefix from this value rather than repeating
          the literal. --}}
    <input type="hidden" name="subject" value="{{#if model.enquiryKind}}{{model.enquiryKind}}{{else}}Course enquiry{{/if}}: {{model.crumb}}">

    <p class="hidden">
      <label>Don&rsquo;t fill this out if you&rsquo;re human: <input name="bot-field"></label>
    </p>

    <fieldset class="rounded-card border border-sand-200 bg-sand-50 px-5 pb-5 pt-2 sm:px-6 sm:pb-6">
      <legend class="px-2 font-display text-lg font-bold text-ink-900">About you</legend>

      <div class="grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <div>
          <label for="enquiry-name" class="block font-medium">
            Your name
          </label>
          <input id="enquiry-name" name="name" type="text" autocomplete="name" required
            class="mt-1 w-full rounded-md border border-sand-300 bg-white px-3 py-2">
        </div>

        <div>
          <label for="enquiry-email" class="block font-medium">
            Email
          </label>
          <input id="enquiry-email" name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" spellcheck="false" required
            class="mt-1 w-full rounded-md border border-sand-300 bg-white px-3 py-2">
        </div>

        <div>
          <label for="enquiry-mobile" class="block font-medium">Mobile number</label>
          <input id="enquiry-mobile" name="mobile" type="tel" autocomplete="tel" required
            class="mt-1 w-full rounded-md border border-sand-300 bg-white px-3 py-2">
          {{!-- The consultation pages render this same form, where there is no
                class and no group to be added to. --}}
          <p class="mt-1 mb-0 text-sm text-ink-500">{{#if model.enquiryKind}}So Gaynor can reach you quickly.{{else}}So Gaynor can add you to the class WhatsApp group.{{/if}}</p>
        </div>

        {{!-- Replies go out by email, text or WhatsApp; asking which saves the
              round trip where a message sits unread in the wrong channel. A
              role="radiogroup" rather than a nested <fieldset>, so the group
              carries an accessible name without a second legend competing
              visually with "About you". --}}
        <div role="radiogroup" aria-labelledby="enquiry-reply-by-label" class="sm:col-span-2">
          <span id="enquiry-reply-by-label" class="block font-medium">How should Gaynor reply?</span>
          <div class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-2">
            <label class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 font-normal">
              <input type="radio" name="reply-by" value="Email" required class="size-4"> Email
            </label>
            <label class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 font-normal">
              <input type="radio" name="reply-by" value="Text or WhatsApp" required class="size-4"> Text or WhatsApp
            </label>
            <label class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 font-normal">
              <input type="radio" name="reply-by" value="Phone call" required class="size-4"> Phone call
            </label>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </fieldset>

    <fieldset class="rounded-card border border-sand-200 bg-sand-50 px-5 pb-5 pt-2 sm:px-6 sm:pb-6">
      <legend class="px-2 font-display text-lg font-bold text-ink-900">About your dog</legend>

      <div class="grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <div>
          <label for="enquiry-dog-name" class="block font-medium">
            Your dog&rsquo;s name
          </label>
          <input id="enquiry-dog-name" name="dog-name" type="text" required
            class="mt-1 w-full rounded-md border border-sand-300 bg-white px-3 py-2">
        </div>

        <div>
          <label for="enquiry-dog-age" class="block font-medium">
            Your dog&rsquo;s age
          </label>
          <input id="enquiry-dog-age" name="dog-age" type="text" placeholder="e.g. 7 months" required
            class="mt-1 w-full rounded-md border border-sand-300 bg-white px-3 py-2">
          <p class="mt-1 mb-0 text-sm text-ink-500">Roughly is fine.{{#unless model.enquiryKind}} It decides which course suits.{{/unless}}</p>
        </div>

        {{!-- Puppy Socialisation only: the vet decides when a puppy can mix,
              and practices differ, so the date is the one thing Gaynor needs
              before she can offer a class. Everywhere else the field is a
              hidden empty twin — Netlify fixes a form's field set from ONE
              parsed instance at deploy time and silently drops names it did
              not see there, so every instance of this form must declare the
              same names or the field goes missing site-wide. --}}
        {{#if model.askVetDate}}
        <div class="sm:col-span-2">
          <label for="enquiry-vet-date" class="block font-medium">
            When your vet says your puppy can mix with other dogs
          </label>
          <input id="enquiry-vet-date" name="vet-date" type="text" placeholder="e.g. 20 October, or not sure yet"
            class="mt-1 w-full rounded-md border border-sand-300 bg-white px-3 py-2">
          <p class="mt-1 mb-0 text-sm text-ink-500">
            Optional. Ask your vet &mdash; some say a week after a jab, some two &mdash; then bring the vet card to the first class.
          </p>
        </div>
        {{else}}
        <input type="hidden" name="vet-date" value="">
        {{/if}}
      </div>
    </fieldset>

    <div>
      <label for="enquiry-message" class="block font-medium">Anything else?</label>
      <textarea id="enquiry-message" name="message" rows="4"
        class="mt-1 w-full rounded-md border border-sand-300 bg-white px-3 py-2"></textarea>
    </div>

    <div>
      <button type="submit" class="btn btn-accent btn-lg">Send enquiry</button>
      <p class="mt-3 mb-0 text-sm text-ink-500">
        Or call Gaynor on
        <a href="tel:{{config.business.telephone}}" class="font-medium text-brand-700 underline underline-offset-4">{{config.business.telephoneDisplay}}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </form>
</section>
